Bridge2AI-Voice: An ethically-sourced, diverse voice dataset linked to health information - Raw Audio Adult Dataset
Version 4.0.0

Access to and use of this dataset are governed by the Bridge2AI-Voice Data Transfer and Use Agreement (DTUA)
between the University of South Florida Board of Trustees and the recipient institution, approved through
the Synapse access requirement:

    https://www.synapse.org/AccessRequirement:AR_ID=9606868

The signed DTUA is the authoritative text. The summary below does not replace or change it. Section numbers
refer to the DTUA.

  - Purpose: commercial or non-commercial research, for the project approved under your agreement.
    Commercialization of the data is not permitted (section 2).
  - Use the data only for the approved project, and only by the personnel listed in Attachment 3.
    Collaborators at other organizations, and other research teams at the same organization, must apply
    and sign their own DTUA (section 3).
  - Do not disclose, release, sell, rent, lease, loan or otherwise give access to the data to any third
    party; keep administrative, technical and physical safeguards (section 4; Attachment 2, sections 6 and 9).
  - Acknowledge the provider as the source of the data in publications and other public disclosures
    (section 7).
  - The data are personally identifiable information and are covered by a Certificate of Confidentiality
    (Attachment 2, section 1).
  - Do not use the data, alone or with other information, to contact participants without IRB approval,
    the provider's written approval and, where required, the participant's informed consent (Attachment 2,
    section 5). Report any unauthorized use or disclosure within five business days of discovery
    (Attachment 2, section 4).
  - When the agreement ends (two years after its start date, when the project ends, on termination, or when
    its ethics approval expires, whichever comes first), destroy the data as the provider instructs and
    certify the destruction in writing within 30 days (Attachment 1, section 4). One copy may be kept where
    records-retention or research-integrity requirements need it, under the same restrictions (section 8).

Questions about data access: B2AI-Voice DACO, daco@b2ai-voice.org
Technical help with Synapse: Synapse Access & Compliance Team, act@sagebase.org

The feature-only release of this dataset on PhysioNet is available under a separate agreement, shown on its
PhysioNet page.
